From ee76a9e5ac03c17809738749501f025c00cc18c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AddledAnorak <ee3230967@iitd.ac.in>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:10:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mgc: add a minimal software-winsys Gallium driver skeleton +
 NIR backend

New driver at src/gallium/drivers/mgc/, selected via GALLIUM_DRIVER=mgc,
targeting the MGC-FP16-v1 micro-GPU (see /docs/isa/isa.yaml in the parent
project). Modeled on softpipe but reduced to the minimum needed to reach
shader compilation over a surfaceless EGL device -- no rasterization, no
real resource storage, no draw module (see mgc_screen.h's scope note and
/docs/driver/gallium-integration.md).

mgc_compiler.c is the NIR -> MGC assembly text backend: the "Direct"
arithmetic subset from the parent project's nir_opcode_triage.md
(fadd/fsub/fmul/fdiv/fneg/fabs/fmin/fmax/mov), scalar constants inlined
against the 8-entry constant bank where they match, one register per SSA
def with no reuse (a documented non-decision, not an oversight -- real
allocation is later scope), and a conservative wait_* after every
producer with a latency class. Emits text, not binary, so the existing
Python mgcasm/mgcsim toolchain in the parent project is the verification
path with no new tooling needed.

Five wiring edits follow the softpipe registration pattern exactly:
meson.options (add 'mgc' to gallium-drivers choices), meson.build
(with_gallium_mgc, folded into with_gallium_swrast), src/gallium/
meson.build (subdir + driver_swrast dependency), and sw_helper.h (the
GALLIUM_MGC screen-creation dispatch, deliberately not matched by the
empty-driver-name fallback or added to the softpipe/llvmpipe fallback
list, so GALLIUM_DRIVER=mgc fails cleanly instead of silently falling
back to another driver on error).

mgc_test_arith.c is a standalone NIR-builder-based unit test for
mgc_compile_nir(), bypassing GLSL entirely -- GLSL constant-folds
pure-literal arithmetic before it reaches any driver, so this is the only
way to exercise a real multi-instruction fmul16/fadd16/fdiv16 chain with
wait_* insertion in isolation.

Verified end to end: GALLIUM_DRIVER=mgc creates a GLES2 context over
surfaceless EGL, GL_RENDERER reports "mgc", real GLSL shaders compile to
MGC assembly via create_fs_state, and the emitted text assembles,
round-trips, and executes bit-exact in the parent project's mgcsim with
no LatencyViolation (see its tests/test_backend_e2e.py). softpipe is
unaffected and still renders correctly as the reference oracle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
